# cheat-on-content — content project .gitignore
# Generated by /cheat-init. Purpose: protect account credentials + local state, while letting your
# creative artifacts (predictions/ videos/ scripts/ etc.) enter version control normally — principles
# #1/#3 rely on git history as the immutable archive of predictions, so those directories are NOT ignored.
#
# Note: comments in .gitignore must occupy their own line; an inline `#` is not a comment (it becomes part of the pattern).

# ── Credentials / login state: never commit (committing equals leaking the account) ──
# .auth/ = Douyin Playwright login state (contains sessionid)
# .auth-xhs/ = Xiaohongshu Playwright login state (contains web_session etc.)
# .auth-linkedin/ = LinkedIn Playwright login state (contains li_at)
# .auth-wechat-channels/ = WeChat Channels assistant Playwright login state
# .cheat-secrets.json = API keys / cookies
.auth/
.auth-xhs/
.auth-linkedin/
.auth-wechat-channels/
.cheat-secrets.json

# ── Local cache and generated artifacts ──
# .cheat-cache = usage logs / trend dedup cache; .cheat-hooks = hook copies generated by init; .debug = adapter debug output
.cheat-cache/
.cheat-hooks/
.debug/

# ── Claude Code local config (contains machine-specific paths / personal permissions) ──
.claude/

# ── Python (left behind by adapters / tool scripts) ──
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
.python-version

# ── macOS / editors / temp files ──
.DS_Store
._*
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.tmp
*.log
